But requirement: "保留 FastAPI 的 app 对象、现有路由注册结果和端点函数名称" — keep endpoint function names so OpenAPI operation IDs and direct endpoint tests keep working. So each endpoint function must still exist as a module-level function with the same name. If we generate them via a factory, the function names would be the factory's inner name unless we set `__name__`. FastAPI uses `endpoint.__name__` for operation_id by default. So we can generate and assign `endpoint.__name__ = "compile_rules_endpoint"` etc. But "端点直接测试继续可用" — direct endpoint tests import e.g. `app.compile_rules_endpoint` and call it. If we do `compile_rules_endpoint = _make_endpoint(...)` at module level, that works as a module attribute.

But wait — existing tests may call these endpoints directly. Let me check the existing tests to see how they test. Also check test for OpenAPI operation ids.

